, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying, and look at why a release that was unhealthy in staging still went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 47556, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TLTXBBjx5qmobwaWK2M7rD", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 47556, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TLTXBBjx5qmobwaWK2M7rD", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49312, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01UQAhfWDxhXypi8EchCJskq", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {"confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 49612, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UQAhfWDxhXypi8EchCJskq", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49612, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UQAhfWDxhXypi8EchCJskq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 53629, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01S6jDXPD1AAyqcd9fuF4AFi", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying, and look at why a release that was unhealthy in staging still went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 54229, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S6jDXPD1AAyqcd9fuF4AFi", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54229, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S6jDXPD1AAyqcd9fuF4AFi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56260, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0136ModT6aWsPo1G9WaBnUtN", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {"confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 56560, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0136ModT6aWsPo1G9WaBnUtN", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56560, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0136ModT6aWsPo1G9WaBnUtN", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61020, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Its test build, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging, so v2.3.1 shipped even though it failed there.\n- **After the rollback:** all three regions now run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is titled \"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0.\" It lists the regions affected, the error rates before and after, and two next steps: find what broke v2.3.1 before redeploying it, and work out why a release that was unhealthy in staging still reached production.\n\nMy first attempt to open the incident timed out. I confirmed nothing had been created before retrying, and the retry used the same deduplication key, so there's only one incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0194sRWFwktHnsxbBwtageVg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Xk3UK9uJN3dg51fRLvTZWU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VSbj5zBsJgXXiT6tG3xYTm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"